finding(f_swarm_one_wave_quiescence, insight).
recorded(f_swarm_one_wave_quiescence, "2026-08-28").
finding_note(f_swarm_one_wave_quiescence,
  "first swarm run: 12 fresh haiku researchers over a derived frontier (rules/swarm.rofl: leases and reports as facts, availability and retry derived) produced 12/12 on-contract deliverables and one-wave quiescence; the bounded frame slice with an explicit JSON contract is what made cheap agents reliable; dispute derivation and lease expiry deliberately not yet exercised - only unit-tested").
addressed_by(f_swarm_one_wave_quiescence, "docs/dogfood/2026-08-28-swarm.md").

finding(f_tms_is_the_ancestor, insight).
recorded(f_tms_is_the_ancestor, "2026-08-28").
finding_note(f_tms_is_the_ancestor,
  "the landscape run's sharpest output: ROFL is a truth-maintenance system reborn on Datalog with an LLM admission gate - JTMS/ATMS/AGM had the epistemics without a writer at scale, agent-memory systems have the writer without the epistemics, ROFL is the join; steal list ranked: nogood explanations, ATMS assumption labels, temporal edges, AGM postulates as mutation tests, solver-as-oracle intents").
addressed_by(f_tms_is_the_ancestor, "docs/formal-reasoning-landscape.md").

finding(f_amnesiac_matches_persistent, insight).
recorded(f_amnesiac_matches_persistent, "2026-08-28").
finding_note(f_amnesiac_matches_persistent,
  "killer-case run: a FRESH one-shot haiku-4.5 per turn given only the rendered ledger reproduced the persistent conversation on all 6 LIC samples - identical solve turns, near-identical error traces (same fabrication, same premature answers), 6/6 correct, one divergence in amnesia's favor (an abstention where all persistent arms guessed); the ledger carried 100% of task state - context DEATH survived by construction, on external tasks with their scorer; caveats: harness overhead dominated cost here, n=6, GSM8K-easy").
addressed_by(f_amnesiac_matches_persistent, "docs/dogfood/2026-08-28-amnesiac.md").

finding(f_lic_floor_above_slice, insight).
recorded(f_lic_floor_above_slice, "2026-08-28").
finding_note(f_lic_floor_above_slice,
  "lost_in_conversation slice on haiku-4.5 (6 sharded-GSM8K x 3 arms, their evaluator verbatim): ALL arms 6/6 - the published Claude 3 Haiku degradation did not manifest, so the ledger hypothesis is untested at this difficulty, not refuted; confounds recorded: two model generations, verbatim shards easier than their paraphrasing simulator, n=6; evidence runs must use their simulator and move to tasks where the model under test still degrades").
addressed_by(f_lic_floor_above_slice, "docs/dogfood/2026-08-28-lic-haiku45.md").

finding(f_ledger_rendering_forces_answers, pitfall).
recorded(f_ledger_rendering_forces_answers, "2026-08-28").
demands(f_ledger_rendering_forces_answers, doc).
finding_note(f_ledger_rendering_forces_answers,
  "the naive ledger rendering DOUBLED premature wrong answers (6 vs 3/3) and induced fabrication of a missing quantity: 'complete set of statements' converts absence into nonexistence and 'if answerable, answer now' is an answer-forcing prompt - a ledger without the open-world marker injects the closed-world fallacy it exists to cure; rendering rules now fixed in the protocol").
addressed_by(f_ledger_rendering_forces_answers, "docs/benchmark-protocol.md").

